# Export whitelist for libtaosnative.so (GNU ld, Linux only).
#
# DO NOT edit by hand: regenerate with
#   python3 source/taos-community/cmake/gen_export_ver.py <build_dir>
#
# Union of: what in-package consumers import (scanned from both linked
# objects and target object files), the DLL_EXPORT public C API
# (include/client/taos.h), taos_* helpers used by out-of-tree connectors,
# and every symbol already listed here (the list is MONOTONIC: regenerating
# from a tree with fewer consumers can only add, never hide).
#
# Needs are configuration dependent (Release drops taosAssertDebug with
# NDEBUG; Debug keeps the tmsg.h wrappers calling tEncodeTSma/tDecodeTSma;
# BUILD_TEST=ON adds the TMQ API consumers), so regenerate/--check in every
# configuration that is built -- monotonicity makes them converge on one
# union instead of fighting each other.
#
# Keeping this list complete matters: the CLI tools resolve engine symbols
# from this library, so a hidden symbol either fails their link or, worse,
# gets satisfied from a local static archive -- embedding a second copy of
# the engine and splitting its global state.
